        "original_id": "89d0c535-eef4-5dec-9d69-415ea143f5e3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Year Books\n- People: Edward I of England, Henry VIII\n- Topics: English law reports, reigns of English monarchs\n\nFacts:\n- The Year Books are the modern English name typically given to the earliest law reports of England.\n- The Year Books survive in a continuous series from 1268 to 1535.\n- The Year Books cover the reigns of English monarchs from Edward I to Henry VIII.\n- Edward I of England was born on 17/18 June 1239 and died on 7 July 1307.\n- Edward I of England was also known as Edward Longshanks and the Hammer of the Scots.\n- Edward I of England was King of England from 1272 to 1307.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
